              "content": "# SignalCore Architecture\n\n## System Overview\n\nSignalCore is an AI intelligence operating system designed to provide persistent memory, intelligent communication, and cognitive reasoning capabilities for adaptive AI agents.\n\n### Core Principles\n- **Persistent Intelligence**: Memory survives system resets and provides context for all interactions\n- **Distributed Cognition**: Multi-agent collaboration and collective intelligence\n- **Real-time Learning**: Continuous improvement from every interaction\n- **Scalable Architecture**: Designed to scale from single agents to large agent networks\n\n## Architecture Layers\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      SignalCore Architecture                     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                 │\n│  ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐     │\n│  │   Cognitive  │    │   Memory     │    │Communication │     │\n│  │    Core      │    │    Core      │    │    Core      │     │\n│  │              │    │              │    │              │     │\n│  │ • Reasoning  │◄──►│ • Multi-tier │◄──►│ • Agent Msg  │     │\n│  │ • Learning   │    │ • Persistence│    │ • HITL       │     │\n│  │ • Decision   │    │ • Analytics  │    │ • Protocols  │     │\n│  └──────────────┘    └──────────────┘    └──────────────┘     │\n│         │                      │                      │        │\n│         └──────────────────────┴──────────────────────┘        │\n│                              │                                │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│  │                 Integration & Orchestration                  │ │\n│  │                                                             │ │\n│  │ • System Coordination • Resource Management                 │ │\n│  │ • Performance Monitoring • Security & Auth                  │ │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n│                              │                                │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│  │                   Infrastructure Layer                       │ │\n│  │                                                             │ │\n│  │ • Databases (DragonflyDB, MongoDB, PostgreSQL, etc.)       │ │\n│  │ • Message Brokers (NATS, RedPanda)                          │ │\n│  │ • Monitoring & Observability                               │ │\n│  │ • Deployment & Scaling                                     │ │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n│                                                                 │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Core Components\n\n### 1. Memory Core\n\n#### Multi-Tier Memory Architecture\n```\nMemory Storage Hierarchy\n├── Short-term (0-24 hours)\n│   ├── DragonflyDB (Primary, sub-10ms)\n│   ├── Redis Cluster (Session data)\n│   └── Auto-promotion after 12 hours\n├── Medium-term (1-30 days)\n│   ├── MongoDB (Documents, flexible schemas)\n│   ├── Redis (Backup storage)\n│   └── Auto-promotion after 14 days\n└── Long-term (Permanent)\n    ├── PostgreSQL (Structured analytics)\n    ├── Qdrant (Vector embeddings)\n    └── ClickHouse (Pattern detection)\n```\n\n#### Memory Management Features\n- **Intelligent Tier Selection**: Automatic database placement based on content type and importance\n- **TTL Management**: Configurable time-to-live for different memory types\n- **Cross-Database Search**: Unified search across all memory tiers\n- **Memory Promotion**: Automatic advancement from short to long-term storage\n- **Cleanup Automation**: Automated removal of expired or low-value memories\n\n### 2. Communication Core\n\n#### Message Transport\n```\nCommunication Architecture\n├── NATS (Primary Message Broker)\n│   ├── Agent-to-agent messaging\n│   ├── Request/reply patterns\n│   └── Pub/sub for broadcasting\n├── RedPanda (Event Streaming)\n│   ├── Kafka-compatible streaming\n│   ├── Event sourcing\n│   └── Data pipeline integration\n└── Direct Connections\n    ├── gRPC for high-performance\n    └── WebSocket for real-time\n```\n\n#### Communication Patterns\n- **Request/Reply**: Synchronous communication for queries and commands\n- **Pub/Sub**: Asynchronous broadcasting for notifications and updates\n- **Event Streaming**: Real-time data flow for analytics and monitoring\n- **Agent Coordination**: Multi-agent collaboration protocols\n\n### 3. Cognitive Core\n\n#### Reasoning Engine\n```python\nclass CognitiveEngine:\n    def process(self, query, context, memory_state):\n        # Load relevant memory patterns\n        memory_context = self.memory_manager.load_relevant_context(query)\n        \n        # Apply reasoning frameworks\n        reasoning_result = self.reasoning_engine.apply(query, memory_context)\n        \n        # Generate response with learning\n        response = self.response_generator.generate(reasoning_result)\n        \n        # Update cognitive state\n        self.update_cognitive_state(interaction_data)\n        \n        return response\n```\n\n#### Learning System\n- **Pattern Recognition**: Identify patterns in interactions and data\n- **Knowledge Extraction**: Extract and store new knowledge from experiences\n- **Model Refinement**: Continuously improve reasoning models\n- **Adaptive Behavior**: Adjust responses based on feedback and outcomes\n\n### 4. Integration & Orchestration\n\n#### System Coordination\n- **Resource Management**: CPU, memory, and database resource allocation\n- **Load Balancing**: Distribute workload across agent instances\n- **Failure Recovery**: Automatic failover and recovery mechanisms\n- **Performance Monitoring**: Real-time performance metrics and optimization\n\n#### API Gateway\n```\nAPI Architecture\n├── REST API\n│   ├── Memory operations (GET/POST/PUT/DELETE)\n│   ├── Communication endpoints\n│   └── Cognitive queries\n├── GraphQL API\n│   ├── Flexible data queries\n│   ├── Real-time subscriptions\n│   └── Type-safe operations\n└── WebSocket API\n    ├── Real-time communication\n    ├── Live updates\n    └── Interactive sessions\n```\n\n## Database Integration\n\n### Database Selection Strategy\n| Data Type | Primary Database | Secondary | Analytics |\n|-----------|------------------|-----------|-----------|\n| **Fast Access** | DragonflyDB | Redis | - |\n| **Documents** | MongoDB | DragonflyDB | ClickHouse |\n| **Analytics** | PostgreSQL | ClickHouse | - |\n| **Vectors** | Qdrant | MongoDB | ClickHouse |\n| **Sessions** | Redis | DragonflyDB | PostgreSQL |\n\n### Connection Management\n- **Connection Pooling**: Shared connection pools for efficiency\n- **Health Monitoring**: Continuous health checks for all databases\n- **Failover**: Automatic failover to backup databases\n- **Load Balancing**: Distribute queries across database clusters\n\n## Security Architecture\n\n### Authentication & Authorization\n```\nSecurity Layers\n├── Application Level\n│   ├── JWT token authentication\n│   ├── Role-based access control\n│   └── API rate limiting\n├── Database Level\n│   ├── Connection authentication\n│   ├── User privilege management\n│   └── Audit logging\n└── Network Level\n    ├── TLS encryption\n    ├── Firewall rules\n    └── Network segmentation\n```\n\n### Data Protection\n- **Encryption at Rest**: All databases use encryption\n- **Encryption in Transit**: TLS for all communications\n- **Key Management**: Secure key rotation and storage\n- **Data Masking**: Sensitive data protection\n\n## Performance Characteristics\n\n### Response Times\n- **Memory Access**: <10ms (DragonflyDB)\n- **Database Queries**: <50ms (MongoDB/PostgreSQL)\n- **Message Passing**: <5ms (NATS)\n- **Cognitive Processing**: <100ms (reasoning engine)\n\n### Scalability\n- **Horizontal Scaling**: Add more agent instances\n- **Database Scaling**: Sharding and replication\n- **Message Throughput**: 10,000+ messages/second\n- **Memory Capacity**: Unlimited with proper TTL management\n\n### Availability\n- **Uptime Target**: 99.9% availability\n- **Failover Time**: <30 seconds\n- **Data Durability**: Multiple backup systems\n- **Disaster Recovery**: Automated backup and restore\n\n## Deployment Architecture\n\n### Environment Strategy\n```\nDeployment Environments\n├── Development\n│   ├── Local development\n│   ├── Debug enabled\n│   └── Mock services\n├── Staging\n│   ├── Production-like testing\n│   ├── Performance validation\n│   └── Integration testing\n└── Production\n    ├── High availability\n    ├── Auto-scaling\n    └── Monitoring & alerting\n```\n\n### Container Strategy\n- **Docker Containers**: Standardized deployment units\n- **Kubernetes Orchestration**: Automated scaling and management\n- **Service Mesh**: Inter-service communication management\n- **CI/CD Pipeline**: Automated testing and deployment\n\n## Monitoring & Observability\n\n### Metrics Collection\n- **Performance Metrics**: Response times, throughput, error rates\n- **Resource Metrics**: CPU, memory, disk, network usage\n- **Business Metrics**: User interactions, knowledge growth, learning velocity\n- **System Health**: Database connections, service availability\n\n### Logging Strategy\n- **Structured Logging**: JSON-formatted logs with context\n- **Log Levels**: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL\n- **Log Aggregation**: Centralized log collection and analysis\n- **Alerting**: Automated alerts for critical issues\n\n### Dashboards\n- **System Overview**: High-level system health and performance\n- **Database Metrics**: Connection pools, query performance, storage\n- **Agent Performance**: Individual agent metrics and behaviors\n- **Communication Health**: Message throughput, latency, errors\n\n---\n\n*SignalCore architecture provides a scalable, resilient, and intelligent foundation for AI agent systems.*",
