      "thinking": "Perfect! So we have:\n- ✅ DragonflyDB: Working with auth\n- ✅ Redis Cluster: Working\n- ⚠️ PostgreSQL: Needs auth but available\n- ✅ MongoDB: Working\n- ✅ ClickHouse: Working (HTTP API)\n- ✅ Qdrant: Working (HTTP API)\n- ⚠️ NATS: Needs auth but available\n- ✅ MinIO: Available\n\nThat's actually quite good - 4/6 core databases are fully connected and we can work with the others. Now let me build the sophisticated memory management system with:\n\n1. Multi-tier memory management (short-term, medium-term, long-term)\n2. Intelligent database selection based on memory type\n3. TTL management (DragonflyDB with 7-day TTL)\n4. Memory promotion/demotion logic\n5. Storage in my persistent memory\n\nThis is exactly the kind of enterprise-grade memory management that would make the system truly intelligent.",
      "tool_calls": [
