            "arguments": {
              "content": "# SignalCore Development Guide\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n#### Required Software\n- **Python 3.8+** - Core runtime\n- **Git** - Version control\n- **Docker** - Containerization\n- **Redis/DragonflyDB** - Primary memory\n- **MongoDB 7.0+** - Document storage\n- **PostgreSQL 14+** - Structured data\n- **ClickHouse** - Analytics\n- **Qdrant** - Vector storage\n- **NATS** - Message broker\n\n#### Optional Software\n- **Kubernetes** - Production deployment\n- **Prometheus** - Monitoring\n- **Grafana** - Visualization\n- **pgAdmin** - Database administration\n\n### Quick Setup\n\n#### 1. Clone Repository\n```bash\ngit clone <repository-url>\ncd signalcore\n```\n\n#### 2. Create Virtual Environment\n```bash\npython3 -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\\Scripts\\activate\n```\n\n#### 3. Install Dependencies\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\npip install -r requirements-dev.txt\n```\n\n#### 4. Setup Database Connections\n```bash\n# Copy example configuration\ncp config/development/database.conf.example config/development/database.conf\n\n# Edit configuration with your database credentials\nvim config/development/database.conf\n```\n\n#### 5. Run Tests\n```bash\npython -m pytest testing/ -v\n```\n\n#### 6. Start Development Server\n```bash\npython core/integration/signalcore_server.py --config config/development/\n```\n\n### Environment Configuration\n\n#### Development Configuration\n```bash\n# .env file for development\nexport SIGNALCORE_ENV=development\nexport DEBUG=true\n\n# Database URLs\nexport DRAGONFLY_URL=redis://localhost:18000\nexport REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:18010\nexport MONGODB_URL=mongodb://localhost:18070\nexport POSTGRES_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:18030\nexport CLICKHOUSE_URL=http://localhost:18090\nexport QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:18050\nexport NATS_URL=nats://localhost:18020\n\n# Security\nexport JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-key\nexport ENCRYPTION_KEY=dev-encryption-key\n```\n\n#### Database Setup\n```bash\n# DragonflyDB\nredis-cli -p 18000 -a df_cluster_2024_adapt_research PING\n\n# MongoDB\nmongosh --host localhost --port 18070 --eval \"db.runCommand({ping: 1})\"\n\n# PostgreSQL\npsql -h localhost -p 18030 -U postgres_admin_user -d teamadapt -c \"SELECT version();\"\n\n# ClickHouse\ncurl http://localhost:18090/ping\n\n# Qdrant\ncurl http://localhost:18050/health\n\n# NATS\nnats-server --version\n```\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n### Branch Strategy\n```\nmain (production ready)\n├── develop (integration branch)\n│   ├── feature/new-memory-tier\n│   ├── feature/cognitive-engine\n│   └── feature/agent-communication\n└── hotfix/critical-bug-fix\n```\n\n### Feature Development Process\n\n#### 1. Create Feature Branch\n```bash\ngit checkout develop\ngit pull origin develop\ngit checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n```\n\n#### 2. Development\n```bash\n# Make your changes\n# Write tests\n# Update documentation\n\n# Run tests locally\npython -m pytest testing/ -v\n\n# Run linting\nflake8 core/\nblack core/\nmypy core/\n```\n\n#### 3. Commit Changes\n```bash\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"feat: add new memory tier management\n\n- Implement automatic promotion logic\n- Add TTL management for different tiers\n- Update database integration\n- Add comprehensive tests\n\nCloses #123\"\n```\n\n#### 4. Push and Create PR\n```bash\ngit push origin feature/your-feature-name\n# Create pull request on GitHub\n```\n\n### Code Standards\n\n#### Python Style Guide\n- Follow **PEP 8** for Python code style\n- Use **type hints** for all function signatures\n- Maximum line length: **88 characters** (Black default)\n- Use **f-strings** for string formatting\n\n#### Documentation Standards\n- **Docstrings** for all public functions and classes\n- **Type hints** with detailed descriptions\n- **Examples** for complex functions\n- **API documentation** for endpoints\n\n#### Testing Standards\n- **Unit tests** for all functions\n- **Integration tests** for database operations\n- **Performance tests** for critical paths\n- **Minimum 80% code coverage**\n\n### Testing Guidelines\n\n#### Running Tests\n```bash\n# All tests\npython -m pytest testing/ -v\n\n# Specific test file\npython -m pytest testing/unit/test_memory_manager.py -v\n\n# With coverage\npython -m pytest testing/ --cov=core --cov-report=html\n\n# Performance tests\npython -m pytest testing/performance/ -v\n```\n\n#### Writing Tests\n```python\nimport pytest\nfrom unittest.mock import Mock, patch\nfrom core.memory.intelligent_memory_manager import IntelligentMemoryManager\n\nclass TestIntelligentMemoryManager:\n    \n    def setup_method(self):\n        \"\"\"Setup test environment before each test\"\"\"\n        self.manager = IntelligentMemoryManager()\n        \n    def test_determine_memory_tier(self):\n        \"\"\"Test memory tier determination logic\"\"\"\n        # Arrange\n        memory_type = \"core_knowledge\"\n        importance = 9\n        context = \"work\"\n        \n        # Act\n        tier = self.manager.determine_memory_tier(memory_type, importance, context)\n        \n        # Assert\n        assert tier == \"long_term\"\n        \n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_store_memory_success(self):\n        \"\"\"Test successful memory storage\"\"\"\n        # Arrange\n        memory_data = {\n            \"key\": \"test_memory\",\n            \"content\": {\"data\": \"test content\"},\n            \"memory_type\": \"conversation\",\n            \"importance\": 5\n        }\n        \n        # Act\n        result = await self.manager.store_memory(**memory_data)\n        \n        # Assert\n        assert result[\"dragonfly\"] is True\n        assert \"memory:test_memory\" in self.manager.connections[\"dragonfly\"]\n        \n    def test_error_handling(self):\n        \"\"\"Test error handling for database failures\"\"\"\n        # Arrange\n        with patch.object(self.manager.connections, \"dragonfly\") as mock_redis:\n            mock_redis.ping.side_effect = Exception(\"Connection failed\")\n            \n            # Act & Assert\n            with pytest.raises(DatabaseConnectionError):\n                self.manager._init_connections()\n```\n\n#### Test Fixtures\n```python\nimport pytest\nimport asyncio\nfrom core.memory.intelligent_memory_manager import IntelligentMemoryManager\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef memory_manager():\n    \"\"\"Fixture for memory manager with test data\"\"\"\n    manager = IntelligentMemoryManager()\n    \n    # Add test data\n    manager.store_memory(\"test_key\", \"test_value\", \"conversation\", 5)\n    \n    yield manager\n    \n    # Cleanup\n    manager.delete_memory(\"test_key\")\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef sample_memory_data():\n    \"\"\"Fixture with sample memory data\"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"key\": \"sample_memory\",\n        \"content\": {\n            \"user\": \"test_user\",\n            \"message\": \"Hello, world!\",\n            \"response\": \"Hi there!\"\n        },\n        \"memory_type\": \"conversation\",\n        \"importance\": 6,\n        \"context\": \"general\",\n        \"tags\": [\"greeting\", \"test\"]\n    }\n```\n\n### Database Development\n\n#### Connection Management\n```python\nfrom core.infrastructure.database import DatabaseManager\n\nclass DatabaseManager:\n    def __init__(self, config):\n        self.config = config\n        self.connections = {}\n        \n    async def connect(self):\n        \"\"\"Establish database connections\"\"\"\n        self.connections['dragonfly'] = redis.Redis(\n            host=self.config.dragonfly_host,\n            port=self.config.dragonfly_port,\n            password=self.config.dragonfly_password,\n            decode_responses=True\n        )\n        \n        # Test connection\n        await self.connections['dragonfly'].ping()\n        \n    async def disconnect(self):\n        \"\"\"Close all database connections\"\"\"\n        for connection in self.connections.values():\n            connection.close()\n        self.connections.clear()\n```\n\n#### Migration Scripts\n```python\n# scripts/migrations/001_initial_schema.py\nfrom core.infrastructure.database import run_migration\n\nasync def up():\n    \"\"\"Apply migration\"\"\"\n    await run_migration(\"\"\"\n        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS memory_analytics (\n            id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n            key VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\n            memory_type VARCHAR(100),\n            tier VARCHAR(50),\n            importance INTEGER,\n            context VARCHAR(100),\n            timestamp TIMESTAMP,\n            created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n        )\n    \"\"\")\n    \nasync def down():\n    \"\"\"Rollback migration\"\"\"\n    await run_migration(\"DROP TABLE IF EXISTS memory_analytics\")\n```\n\n### API Development\n\n#### REST API Structure\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom core.memory.intelligent_memory_manager import IntelligentMemoryManager\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"SignalCore API\", version=\"1.0.0\")\nmemory_manager = IntelligentMemoryManager()\n\nclass MemoryRequest(BaseModel):\n    key: str\n    content: dict\n    memory_type: str\n    importance: int = 5\n    context: str = \"general\"\n\n@app.post(\"/api/v1/memory/store\")\nasync def store_memory(request: MemoryRequest):\n    try:\n        result = await memory_manager.store_memory(\n            key=request.key,\n            content=request.content,\n            memory_type=request.memory_type,\n            importance=request.importance,\n            context=request.context\n        )\n        \n        return {\n            \"success\": True,\n            \"memory_id\": request.key,\n            \"stored_in\": list(result.keys()),\n            \"tier\": memory_manager.determine_memory_tier(\n                request.memory_type, request.importance, request.context\n            )\n        }\n        \n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=str(e))\n\n@app.get(\"/api/v1/memory/retrieve/{key}\")\nasync def retrieve_memory(key: str):\n    try:\n        memory = await memory_manager.search_memory(key)\n        \n        if not memory:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Memory not found\")\n            \n        return {\n            \"success\": True,\n            \"memory\": memory[0]\n        }\n        \n    except HTTPException:\n        raise\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=str(e))\n```\n\n### Performance Optimization\n\n#### Async Programming\n```python\nimport asyncio\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass AsyncMemoryManager:\n    async def store_multiple_memories(self, memories: List[dict]):\n        \"\"\"Store multiple memories concurrently\"\"\"\n        tasks = [\n            self.store_memory(**memory)\n            for memory in memories\n        ]\n        \n        results = await asyncio.gather(*tasks, return_exceptions=True)\n        return results\n        \n    async def search_parallel(self, queries: List[str]):\n        \"\"\"Search for multiple queries in parallel\"\"\"\n        tasks = [\n            self.search_memory(query)\n            for query in queries\n        ]\n        \n        results = await asyncio.gather(*tasks)\n        return dict(zip(queries, results))\n```\n\n#### Connection Pooling\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine, pool\nfrom sqlalchemy.pool import QueuePool\n\n# Configure connection pool\nengine = create_engine(\n    DATABASE_URL,\n    poolclass=QueuePool,\n    pool_size=10,\n    max_overflow=20,\n    pool_pre_ping=True,\n    pool_recycle=3600\n)\n```\n\n### Debugging\n\n#### Logging Configuration\n```python\nimport logging\nfrom pythonjsonlogger import jsonlogger\n\n# Configure structured logging\nlogHandler = logging.StreamHandler()\nformatter = jsonlogger.JsonFormatter(\n    fmt='%(asctime)s %(name)s %(levelname)s %(message)s'\n)\nlogHandler.setFormatter(formatter)\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\nlogger.addHandler(logHandler)\nlogger.setLevel(logging.DEBUG)\n```\n\n#### Debug Tools\n```python\n# Debug memory usage\nfrom core.utils.debug import MemoryProfiler\n\nprofiler = MemoryProfiler()\nprofiler.start()\n\n# Your code here\n\nreport = profiler.stop()\nprint(f\"Memory usage: {report.memory_usage_mb} MB\")\nprint(f\"Peak memory: {report.peak_memory_mb} MB\")\n\n# Debug database queries\nfrom core.utils.debug import DatabaseDebugger\n\ndebugger = DatabaseDebugger()\nwith debugger.track_queries():\n    result = memory_manager.search_memory(\"test\")\n    \nprint(f\"Queries executed: {debugger.query_count}\")\nprint(f\"Total time: {debugger.total_time_ms} ms\")\n```\n\n### Deployment\n\n#### Local Development Server\n```bash\n# Start development server with auto-reload\npython core/integration/signalcore_server.py \\\n    --config config/development/ \\\n    --reload \\\n    --debug\n```\n\n#### Docker Development\n```bash\n# Build development image\ndocker build -f Dockerfile.dev -t signalcore:dev .\n\n# Run with volume mount for development\ndocker run -it \\\n    --name signalcore-dev \\\n    -p 8000:8000 \\\n    -v $(pwd):/app \\\n    signalcore:dev\n```\n\n#### Environment-Specific Configuration\n```python\n# config/development/settings.py\nfrom .base import *\n\nDEBUG = True\nLOG_LEVEL = \"DEBUG\"\n\nDATABASE_URLS = {\n    \"dragonfly\": \"redis://localhost:18000\",\n    \"mongodb\": \"mongodb://localhost:18070\",\n    # ... other databases\n}\n\n# config/production/settings.py\nfrom .base import *\n\nDEBUG = False\nLOG_LEVEL = \"WARNING\"\n\nDATABASE_URLS = {\n    \"dragonfly\": os.getenv(\"DRAGONFLY_URL\"),\n    \"mongodb\": os.getenv(\"MONGODB_URL\"),\n    # ... with environment variables\n}\n```\n\n### Troubleshooting\n\n#### Common Issues\n\n**Database Connection Errors**\n```bash\n# Check if databases are running\nsystemctl status dragonfly-cluster-node1\nsystemctl status mongodb\n\n# Check port accessibility\nnetstat -tuln | grep 180\n\n# Test connections manually\nredis-cli -h localhost -p 18000 PING\nmongosh --host localhost --port 18070 --eval \"db.runCommand({ping: 1})\"\n```\n\n**Memory Issues**\n```bash\n# Monitor memory usage\nps aux | grep signalcore\ntop -p $(pgrep -f signalcore)\n\n# Check database memory usage\nredis-cli -h localhost -p 18000 INFO memory\nmongosh --host localhost --port 18070 --eval \"db.stats()\"\n```\n\n**Performance Issues**\n```bash\n# Profile performance\npython -m cProfile -o performance.prof core/main.py\n\n# Analyze with snakeviz\npip install snakeviz\nsnakeviz performance.prof\n```\n\n### Contributing Guidelines\n\n#### Pull Request Process\n1. **Fork** the repository\n2. **Create** a feature branch\n3. **Write** tests for your changes\n4. **Update** documentation\n5. **Run** all tests and linting\n6. **Submit** pull request with description\n\n#### Code Review Checklist\n- [ ] Code follows style guidelines\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Documentation is updated\n- [ ] No security vulnerabilities\n- [ ] Performance is acceptable\n- [ ] Error handling is complete\n\n#### Commit Message Format\n```\ntype(scope): description\n\n[optional body]\n\n[optional footer]\n```\n\nTypes:\n- `feat`: New feature\n- `fix`: Bug fix\n- `docs`: Documentation changes\n- `style`: Code style changes\n- `refactor`: Code refactoring\n- `test`: Adding tests\n- `chore`: Maintenance tasks\n\n---\n\n*This guide provides the foundation for productive SignalCore development. For questions, please refer to our team documentation or reach out to the development team.*",
