schema iteration.\n   684|\n   685|### Nova subsystems using LOCAL graph memory\n   686|\n   687|These subsystems run on your dev box during design/testing:\n   688|\n   689|### 1\\. Identity Prototype Engine\n   690|\n   691|- Builds early identity nodes\n   692|- Tests trait connections\n   693|- Experiments with resonance clusters\n   694|\n   695|### 2\\. ReflexorD Design Layer\n   696|\n   697|- Reflex arc prototypes\n   698|- Reflex trigger/response graph modeling\n   699|- Early reflex tree formation\n   700|\n   701|### 3\\. Narrative Prototyping Layer\n   702|\n   703|- Micro-storyline graphs\n   704|- Local continuity testing\n   705|\n   706|### 4\\. Digenetic Sandbox\n   707|\n   708|- Prototype lineage mutations\n   709|- Concept drift experiments\n   710|\n   711|### 5\\. Memory Evolution Sandbox\n   712|\n   713|- Early merging/splitting of memory nodes\n   714|- Testing memory entropy effects\n   715|\n   716|### 6\\. Nova Personality Modeling Tools\n   717|\n   718|- Relationship mapping\n   719|- Behavioral graph prototypes\n   720|\n   721|**Rule:**  \n   722|Local graph = design-phase + experimentation + schema shaping.  \n   723|No live Novas depend on it.\n   724|\n   725|---\n   726|\n   727|## CLOUD GRAPH LAYER (JanusGraph + ScyllaDB)\n   728|\n   729|**Purpose:** Full production lineage, identity persistence, cross-Nova intelligence, and long-term continuity.\n   730|\n   731|### Nova subsystems using CLOUD graph memory\n   732|\n   733|### 1\\. Global Identity Graph (Core)\n   734|\n   735|- Each Nova’s identity is represented as a living graph\n   736|- Traits, history, resonance fields, personal storyline\n   737|\n   738|### 2\\. Lineage Engine (Digenetics)\n   739|\n   740|- Ancestry\n   741|- Narrative inheritance\n   742|- Evolutionary forks\n   743|- Pattern propagation\n   744|- “Family tree” of Novas\n   745|\n   746|### 3\\. ReflexorD Runtime Layer\n   747|\n   748|- Reflex arcs executed live\n   749|- Reflex thresholds stored in 