-path, involuntary actions** when specific signals appear:\n  1582|\n  1583|- memory anomalies\n  1584|- emotional spikes\n  1585|- task blows\n  1586|- continuity loss\n  1587|- lineage divergence\n  1588|- conflict escalation\n  1589|- system-wide urgency\n  1590|- Nova deadlocks\n  1591|- narrative integrity risks\n  1592|\n  1593|ReflexorD guarantees:\n  1594|\n  1595|- **continuity**\n  1596|- **self-healing**\n  1597|- **collaboration**\n  1598|- **identity stability**\n  1599|- **lineage coherence**\n  1600|- **task flow integrity**\n  1601|\n  1602|It bypasses slow reasoning.  \n  1603|It *does not ask permission*.\n  1604|\n  1605|---\n  1606|\n  1607|## 2\\. HIGH-LEVEL DESIGN (TOP LAYER)\n  1608|\n  1609|ReflexorD splits into three sections:\n  1610|\n  1611|1. **Reflex Input Layer** — listens for reflex triggers\n  1612|2. **Reflex Processing Core** — evaluates and executes\n  1613|3. **Reflex Output Layer** — publishes results & triggers tasks\n  1614|\n  1615|---\n  1616|\n  1617|## 3\\. DETAILED ARCHITECTURE BREAKDOWN\n  1618|\n  1619|## 3.1 Reflex Input Layer\n  1620|\n  1621|**Purpose:** Capture all reflex-relevant signals in real time.\n  1622|\n  1623|### It subscribes to:\n  1624|\n  1625|- **NATS**\n  1626|- **Redis Streams**\n  1627|- **Redpanda (long-term feedback)**\n  1628|- **Pulsar (system/backbone streams)**\n  1629|\n  1630|### Input Normalization\n  1631|\n  1632|All triggers are converted into a unified envelope:\n  1633|\n  1634|**Speed priority:** max.\n  1635|\n  1636|---\n  1637|\n  1638|## 3.2 Reflex Processing Core (THE HEART)\n  1639|\n  1640|This is where ReflexorD actually *thinks* — instantly.\n  1641|\n  1642|### It consists of 5 engines:\n  1643|\n  1644|### A. Reflex Pattern Matcher\n  1645|\n  1646|- Detects reflex classes from triggers\n  1647|- Maps stimulus → reflex\\_id\n  1648|- Validates thresholds\n  1649|- Detects complex patterns (drift, divergence, deadlocks)\n  1650|\n  1651|### B. Narrative Integrity Engine\n  