emory:v1.0\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 **Configuration Options for Target Agents**\n\n### **Basic Setup** (Single Database)\n```bash\n# Minimal Redis-based memory\npython3 mini_agent_memory_installer.py --database-config CONFIGS/basic_redis.json\n```\n\n### **Production Setup** (Multi-Database)\n```bash\n# Full enterprise-grade setup\npython3 mini_agent_memory_installer.py --database-config CONFIGS/team_adapt_production.json\n```\n\n### **Custom Setup**\n```bash\n# Custom database configuration\npython3 mini_agent_memory_installer.py --database-config /path/to/custom_config.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📋 **Database Support Matrix**\n\n| Database | Status | Purpose | Port Range |\n|----------|--------|---------|------------|\n| **DragonflyDB** | ✅ Ready | Primary memory, fastest | 18000-18002 |\n| **Redis Cluster** | ✅ Ready | Session data, redundancy | 18010-18012 |\n| **PostgreSQL** | ✅ Ready | Structured analytics | 18030-18032 |\n| **ClickHouse** | ✅ Ready | Pattern detection | 18090 |\n| **MongoDB** | ⚠️ Optional | Document storage | 27017 |\n\n**Target agents can use ANY combination** - the system auto-detects and configures available databases.\n\n---\n\n## 🧪 **Verification Commands** \n\nAfter deployment, verify the memory system works:\n\n```bash\n# Quick test\npython3 session_persistence_demo.py\n\n# Check persistence\nredis-cli -h localhost -p 18000 HGETALL mini_agent:user_preferences\nredis-cli -h localhost -p 18000 HGETALL mini_agent:sessions\n\n# Run health check\npython3 mini_agent_core.py --action health\n\n# Test memory persistence\npython3 -c \"\nfrom mini_agent_core import MiniAgentCore\nmemory = MiniAgentCore()\nmemory.store_knowledge('test_key', 'test_value', 'Test knowledge')\nresult = memory.search_knowledge('test_key')\nprint('Memory working:', result is not None)\n\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🎉 **What Target Mini-Agents Get**\n\nAfter deployment, **every** Mini-Agent will have:\n\n- 🧠 **Permanent memory** across ALL interactions\n- 💾 **Multi-database redundancy** 