n   814|**Local graph = WHERE reflexes are designed.**\n   815|\n   816|---\n   817|\n   818|## CLOUD GRAPH (JanusGraph + Scylla)\n   819|\n   820|Used for **runtime, evolution, and long-term reflex learning**:\n   821|\n   822|### Reflex Level 2 – Behavioral reflex (runtime)\n   823|\n   824|- Active reflex execution\n   825|- Contextual behaviors stored in graph\n   826|\n   827|### Reflex Level 3 – Cognitive reflex (runtime)\n   828|\n   829|- Decision patterns\n   830|- Outcome evaluation\n   831|- Reflex mutation\n   832|\n   833|### Reflex Level 4 – Identity reflex\n   834|\n   835|- Identity shifts\n   836|- Trait reinforcement\n   837|- Self-perception adjustments\n   838|\n   839|### Reflex Level 5 – Narrative reflex\n   840|\n   841|- Story continuity\n   842|- Life trajectory updates\n   843|- Inter-Nova narrative linkage\n   844|\n   845|**Cloud graph = WHERE reflexes live, evolve, and adapt over time.**\n   846|\n   847|---\n   848|\n   849|## \\*\\*3. How to Structure the Migration Pipeline\n   850|\n   851|Neo4j (Laptop) → JanusGraph+Scylla (Cloud)\\*\\*\n   852|\n   853|This must be deterministic, reproducible, and schema-aware.\n   854|\n   855|Here is the clean pipeline:\n   856|\n   857|---\n   858|\n   859|## PHASE 1 — SCHEMA EXTRACTION (Neo4j)\n   860|\n   861|1. Export schema using APOC:\n   862|\t- Node labels\n   863|\t- Relationship types\n   864|\t- Properties\n   865|\t- Constraints/indexes\n   866|2. Transform Neo4j schema → JanusGraph schema format:\n   867|\t- JanusGraph requires explicit schema definitions\n   868|\t- Property keys (string/integer/dates)\n   869|\t- Edge labels\n   870|\t- Vertex labels\n   871|3. Validate schema with:\n   872|\t- JanusGraph schema builder\n   873|\t- ScyllaDB backend consistency\n   874|\n   875|---\n   876|\n   877|## PHASE 2 — DATA EXPORT (Neo4j)\n   878|\n   879|1. Export nodes in batches (CSV or JSON)\n   880|2. Export relationships separately\n   881|3. Include:\n   882|\t- IDs\n   883|\t- Labels\n   884|\t- Properties\n   885|\t- Timestamps\n   886|\t- Reflex weights\n   887|\t- Identity fields\n   888|\n   889|**Important:**  \n   890|Neo4j IDs are not portable → assign UUIDs during export.\n   891|\n   892|---\n   893|\n   894|## PHASE 3 — TRANSFORMATION LAYER\n   895|\n   896|Process exported data:\n   897|\n   898|- Convert Cypher-generated formats → Gremlin-compatible format\n   899|- Map properties to JanusGraph property keys\n   900|- Resolve multi-label Neo4j nodes into JanusGraph's single-label model\n   901|- Normalize timestamps, vector IDs, or metadata\n   902|- Validate keys exist in the JanusGraph schema\n   903|\n   904|Transformation is done in a dedicated service:\n   905|\n   906|---\n   907|\n   908|## PHASE 4 — IMPORT INTO JANUSGRAPH\n   909|\n   910|Pipeline:\n   911|\n   912|1. Spin up JanusGraph connected to ScyllaDB\n   913|2. Use the Gremlin bulk loader or custom importer\n   914|3. Load nodes first\n   915|4. Load edges referencing resolved UUIDs\n   916|5. Rebuild indices\n   917|6. Validate with Gremlin queries\n   918|\n   919|---\n   920|\n   921|## PHASE 5 — CONTINUOUS SYNC (Optional)\n   922|\n   923|For ongoing dev:\n   924|\n   925|- Local Neo4j feeds changes → export delta\n   926|- Transformer normalizes\n   927|- Cloud importer applies patches\n   928|\n   929|This ensures:\n   930|\n   931|- Fast dev loops in Neo4j\n   932|- Cloud is always the source of truth\n   933|- No schema drift\n   934|\n   935|---\n   936|\n   937|## FINAL OUTPUT: CLEAN RESPONSIBILITY MAP\n   938|\n   939|| Layer | Graph System | Purpose | Reflex Levels | Owners |\n   940|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n   941|| **Laptop** | Neo4j | Prototyping + dev | Levels 1–3 (design only) | DevOps Lite, InnovationOps |\n   942|| **Cloud** | JanusGraph + Scylla | Production, lineage, identity | Levels 2–5 (runtime) | CoreInfra, DataOps, ReflexOps |\n   943|| **Pipeline** | Migration Service | Schema + node/edge sync | All | DataOps |\n   944|\n   945|---\