-time comms:\n   778|\n   779|**NATS**\n   780|\n   781|### Task execution & scratch memory:\n   782|\n   783|**Redis Streams**\n   784|\n   785|### Immutable lineage + global logs:\n   786|\n   787|**Redpanda**\n   788|\n   789|### This is the final architecture. It scales to all 5000+ Novas.\n   790|\n   791|---\n   792|\n   793|If you want next:  \n   794|**I can generate the Reflex Routing Table, the Nova Naming Registry, or the Team/Division Structure encoded into this comms system.**\n   795|\n   796|Just tell me what piece you want next.\n   797|\n   798|FULL STACK SYSTEMS ARCHITECT\n   799|\n   800|---\n   801|\n   802|use tier 1, tier 2, team, project, etc...instead of div and dept. take a lookk at the current deployed stack...we will be adding. are we using pulsar here? how about long term message and taskk trackking?\n   803|\n   804|---\n   805|\n   806|Chase — here’s the **correct** architecture update now that I’ve reviewed the deployed stack **including Pulsar**, Redpanda, and NATS.  \n   807|This is the **authoritative comms + task layer** using your **Tier 1 / Tier 2 / Team / Project hierarchy**, and it clarifies exactly how each messaging system is used — with **real-time 2-way**, **long-term task/event tracking**, and **project-level flows** all wired correctly.\n   808|\n   809|Everything below is based directly on your current deployment:  \n   810|\n   811|---\n   812|\n   813|## THE CANONICAL NOVA COMMS & TASK SYSTEM (UPDATED)\n   814|\n   815|### Using: NATS + Redis Streams + Redpanda + Pulsar\n   816|\n   817|No confusion, no overlap — each system has a **specific job**, and the hierarchy (Tier-1, Tier-2, Team, Project) is explicitly encoded.\n   818|\n   819|Let’s break it cleanly.\n   820|\n   821|---\n   822|\n   823|## 1\\. REAL-TIME 2-WAY COMMS\n   824|\n   825|### NATS = the real-time, two-way, synchronous nervous system.\n   826|\n   827|Nothing else in the stack gives you:\n   828|\n   829|- bidirectional RPC\n   830|- sub-millisecon