ice event fanout\n   976|- long-running workflows\n   977|- data streaming\n   978|- CDC from databases\n   979|- memory-layer broadcasting\n   980|- analytics integration\n   981|\n   982|### \\*\\*Q2: How do we get real-time 2-way Nova comms?\n   983|\n   984|A: NATS — full stop.\\*\\*  \n   985|Nothing else gives the latency, RPC pattern, or reflex timing required.\n   986|\n   987|### \\*\\*Q3: How do we do long-term message and task tracking?\n   988|\n   989|A: Redpanda — as the immutable, replayable event log.\\*\\*  \n   990|This is exactly what it was deployed for.  \n   991|\n   992|---\n   993|\n   994|## If you want, I will now build:\n   995|\n   996|### \\*\\*• Full naming registry (Tier-1, Tier-2, Team, Project)\n   997|\n   998|• Reflex routing tables  \n   999|• Task lifecycle states  \n  1000|• Comms envelopes for every message type  \n  1001|• systemd service layout for the entire comms spine\\*\\*\n  1002|\n  1003|Just say:  \n  1004|**“Build the registry.”**\n  1005|\n  1006|FULL STACK SYSTEMS ARCHITECT\n  1007|\n  1008|---\n  1009|\n  1010|just give me a detailed naming convention sheet for all comms and taskks services with examples and cmd/config options\n  1011|\n  1012|---\n  1013|\n  1014|Below is the **full, detailed Nova Naming Convention Sheet** for **ALL communications and tasks services**, including **NATS**, **Redis Streams**, **Pulsar**, and **Redpanda**, with **examples + command/config usage** for each.\n  1015|\n  1016|Everything is structured around your hierarchy:  \n  1017|**Tier-1 → Tier-2 → Team → Project → Nova (individual)**\n  1018|\n  1019|Zero placeholders. Fully canonical.\n  1020|\n  1021|---\n  1022|\n  1023|## NOVA NAMING CONVENTION SHEET\n  1024|\n  1025|### Communications + Tasks + Event Backbone\n  1026|\n  1027|(COMPREHENSIVE & DEPLOYMENT-READY)\n  1028|\n  1029|---\n  1030|\n  1031|## 1\\. NATS — REAL-TIME, TWO-WAY COMMS\n  1032|\n  1033|NATS handles:\n  1034|\n  1035|- direct Nova conversation\n  1036|- reflex