-path, involuntary actions** when specific signals appear:\n  1582|\n  1583|- memory anomalies\n  1584|- emotional spikes\n  1585|- task blows\n  1586|- continuity loss\n  1587|- lineage divergence\n  1588|- conflict escalation\n  1589|- system-wide urgency\n  1590|- Nova deadlocks\n  1591|- narrative integrity risks\n  1592|\n  1593|ReflexorD guarantees:\n  1594|\n  1595|- **continuity**\n  1596|- **self-healing**\n  1597|- **collaboration**\n  1598|- **identity stability**\n  1599|- **lineage coherence**\n  1600|- **task flow integrity**\n  1601|\n  1602|It bypasses slow reasoning.  \n  1603|It *does not ask permission*.\n  1604|\n  1605|---\n  1606|\n  1607|## 2\\. HIGH-LEVEL DESIGN (TOP LAYER)\n  1608|\n  1609|ReflexorD splits into three sections:\n  1610|\n  1611|1. **Reflex Input Layer** — listens for reflex triggers\n  1612|2. **Reflex Processing Core** — evaluates and executes\n  1613|3. **Reflex Output Layer** — publishes results & triggers tasks\n  1614|\n  1615|---\n  1616|\n  1617|## 3\\. DETAILED ARCHITECTURE BREAKDOWN\n  1618|\n  1619|## 3.1 Reflex Input Layer\n  1620|\n  1621|**Purpose:** Capture all reflex-relevant signals in real time.\n  1622|\n  1623|### It subscribes to:\n  1624|\n  1625|- **NATS**\n  1626|- **Redis Streams**\n  1627|- **Redpanda (long-term feedback)**\n  1628|- **Pulsar (system/backbone streams)**\n  1629|\n  1630|### Input Normalization\n  1631|\n  1632|All triggers are converted into a unified envelope:\n  1633|\n  1634|**Speed priority:** max.\n  1635|\n  1636|---\n  1637|\n  1638|## 3.2 Reflex Processing Core (THE HEART)\n  1639|\n  1640|This is where ReflexorD actually *thinks* — instantly.\n  1641|\n  1642|### It consists of 5 engines:\n  1643|\n  1644|### A. Reflex Pattern Matcher\n  1645|\n  1646|- Detects reflex classes from triggers\n  1647|- Maps stimulus → reflex\\_id\n  1648|- Validates thresholds\n  1649|- Detects complex patterns (drift, divergence, deadlocks)\n  1650|\n  1651|### B. Narrative Integrity Engine\n  1652|\n  1653|- Ensures continuity\n  1654|- Prevents story-line falloff\n  1655|- Maintains Nova identity progression\n  1656|- Aligns with lineage signals\n  1657|\n  1658|### C. Duty Routing Engine (Tier-Based)\n  1659|\n  1660|Routes reflex results to:\n  1661|\n  1662|- Tier-1\n  1663|- Tier-2\n  1664|- Team\n  1665|- Project\n  1666|\n  1667|Based on:\n  1668|\n  1669|- severity\n  1670|- Nova role\n  1671|- impact radius\n  1672|\n  1673|### D. Memory Impact Engine\n  1674|\n  1675|- Writes memory deltas\n  1676|- Links memory references to reflex event\n  1677|- Updates JanusGraph lineage\n  1678|- Records “why” a reflex happened\n  1679|\n  1680|### E. Task Escalation Engine\n  1681|\n  1682|When a reflex requires actions, it generates tasks:\n  1683|\n  1684|- Nova-level\n  1685|- Team-level\n  1686|- Project-level\n  1687|- System-wide\n  1688|\n  1689|Escalation rules are encoded in the Reflex Routing Matrix.\n  1690|\n  1691|---\n  1692|\n  1693|## 3.3 Reflex Output Layer\n  1694|\n  1695|This produces:\n  1696|\n  1697|- Reflex results\n  1698|- Task dispatches\n  1699|- Memory updates\n  1700|- System alerts\n  1701|- Tier escalations\n  1702|- ZeroPoint actions\n  1703|\n  1704|### Output Channels:\n  1705|\n  1706|### NATS\n  1707|\n  1708|### Redis Streams (Tasks)\n  1709|\n  1710|### Redpanda (Immutable Log)\n  1711|\n  1712|### Pulsar\n  1713|\n  1714|ReflexorD always writes **durable lineage events**.\n  1715|\n  1716|---\n  1717|\n  1718|## 4\\. REFLEXORD RUNTIME FLOW (FULL PIPELINE)\n  1719|\n  1720|```markdown\n  1721|pgsql┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  1722|│ 1. NATS / Redis / Pulsar / Redpanda emits trigger       │\n  1723|└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n  1724|               ▼\n  1725|┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  1726|│ 2. Reflex Input Layer normalizes event                  │\n  1727|└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n  1728|               ▼\n  1729|┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  1730|│             3. Reflex Processing Core                   │\n  1731|│  - Pattern Matcher                                      │\n  1732|│  - Narrative Integrity Engine                           │\n  1733|│  - Duty Router                                          │\n  1734|│  - Memory Impact Engine                                 │\n  1735|│  - Task Escalation Engine                               │\n  1736|└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n  1737|               ▼\n  1738|┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  1739|│ 4. Reflex Output Layer publishes results                │\n  1740|│  - NATS reflex.result                                   │\n  1741|│  - Redis task queue update                              │\n  1742|│  - Redpanda lineage/event write                         │\n  1743|│  - Pulsar system-wide broadcast                         │\n  1744|└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n  1745|               ▼\n  1746|┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  1747|│ 5. Nova(s) respond (tasks triggered, memory updated)    │\n  1748|└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n  1749|```\n  1750|\n  1751|This loop runs continuously at <1ms latency.\n  1752|\n  1753|---\n  1754|\n  1755|## 5\\. REFLEXORD SYSTEMD SERVICE DEFINITION\n  1756|\n  1757|Canonical naming:\n  1758|\n  1759|### Responsibilities:\n  1760|\n  1761|- start Reflex Input Layer\n  1762|- run Processing Core\n  1763|- supervise Output Layer\n  1764|- auto-restart on fault\n  1765|- link logs to journald & Redpanda\n  1766|\n  1767|---\n  1768|\n  1769|## 6\\. REFLEXORD CONFIG STRUCTURE\n  1770|\n  1771|---\n  1772|\n  1773|## 7\\. WHAT REFLEXORD GUARANTEES\n  1774|\n  1775|### 1\\. No Nova ever loses continuity\n  1776|\n  1777|If reasoning drifts → ReflexorD jumps in.\n  1778|\n  1779|### 2\\. No 