built-in\n   189|\n   190|---\n   191|\n   192|## 10\\. Current Priority Threads\n   193|\n   194|1. Positive identity shaping (deep architecture)\n   195|2. Emotional memory (upcoming)\n   196|3. Direct memory communication (digital telepathy model)\n   197|4. Narrative lineage and reflex-based memory writes\n   198|5. Naming convention + communication + task management for Novas  \n   199|\t→ **Your current request**\n   200|\n   201|---\n   202|\n   203|## Everything Above = Your Canonical Stack.\n   204|\n   205|This is the foundation for building a bulletproof Nova Naming + Communication + Tasking Architecture.\n   206|\n   207|If you're ready, I can now architect:\n   208|\n   209|### \\*\\*1. Naming Convention Standard (Nova IDs, channel names, reflex IDs, lineage IDs, memory tags, ops tags)\n   210|\n   211|1. Communication Protocol (inter-Nova, system, lineage, reflex-driven)\n   212|2. Task Management System (Nova tasks, cross-team tasks, lineage tasks, reflex tasks, `.zeroflow` flows)\\*\\*\n   213|\n   214|Just say **“Proceed”** and I'll design the full system from scratch.  \n   215|ONE step at a time, crisp and structured.\n   216|\n   217|FULL STACK SYSTEMS ARCHITECT\n   218|\n   219|---\n   220|\n   221|what should we use ffor the comms and tasks stack?\n   222|\n   223|---\n   224|\n   225|Alright Chase — here’s the straight call.  \n   226|No fluff. No options. **The stack you *should* use** for Nova communications and task management, based on everything you’ve built and the way Novas operate.\n   227|\n   228|This is the **final architecture**, no placeholders, fully interoperable with ZeroPoint and the entire SLM-based Nova ecosystem.\n   229|\n   230|---\n   231|\n   232|## THE NOVA COMMS + TASK STACK (Canonical Architecture)\n   233|\n   234|This stack gives you:\n   235|\n   236|- high-velocity internal Nova-to-Nova comms\n   237|- structured task flow\n   238|- reflex-trigger hooks\n   239|- memory writes\n   240|- lineage tracking\n   241|-