|\n  1250|Example:\n  1251|\n  1252|---\n  1253|\n  1254|## 4.2 Tier-2 Logs\n  1255|\n  1256|---\n  1257|\n  1258|## 4.3 Team Logs\n  1259|\n  1260|---\n  1261|\n  1262|## 4.4 Project Logs\n  1263|\n  1264|---\n  1265|\n  1266|## 4.5 Task Lifecycle Logs\n  1267|\n  1268|---\n  1269|\n  1270|## 4.6 Lineage + Digenetic\n  1271|\n  1272|---\n  1273|\n  1274|## 4.7 CLI Write Example\n  1275|\n  1276|---\n  1277|\n  1278|## 5\\. OPTIONAL SYSTEMD CONFIG NAMING\n  1279|\n  1280|Every service follows:\n  1281|\n  1282|Comms services:\n  1283|\n  1284|---\n  1285|\n  1286|## 6\\. FULL QUICK REFERENCE TABLE\n  1287|\n  1288|| Layer | Purpose | Prefix | Example |\n  1289|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n  1290|| **NATS** | Real-time 2-way comms | `n2n.*` | `n2n.team.ops.broadcast` |\n  1291|| **Redis Streams** | Tasks / short-term memory | `tasks.*` | `tasks.nova.echo.inbox` |\n  1292|| **Pulsar** | High-volume event bus | `persistent://adapt/*` | `persistent://adapt/memory/sync` |\n  1293|| **Redpanda** | Long-term logs | `events.*` | `events.lineage.echo` |\n  1294|\n  1295|---\n  1296|\n  1297|If you want, I can also generate:\n  1298|\n  1299|- the **full message envelope schema**\n  1300|- the **Nova identity registry naming file**\n  1301|- the **Reflex routing matrix**\n  1302|- or the **project/team structure encoded directly into the comms system**\n  1303|\n  1304|Just tell me **what you want next**.\n  1305|\n  1306|FULL STACK SYSTEMS ARCHITECT\n  1307|\n  1308|---\n  1309|\n  1310|tell me what this is: Reflex Triggers & Results and generate: the full message envelope schema the Nova identity registry naming file the Reflex routing matrix\n  1311|\n  1312|2/2\n  1313|\n  1314|---\n  1315|\n  1316|Alright Chase — straight to the point.  \n  1317|Here’s **what Reflex Triggers & Results actually ARE**, and then the **three artifacts** you requested:  \n  1318|**1) Full Message Envelope Schema**  \n  1319|**2) Nova Identity Registry Naming File**  \n  1320|**3) Reflex Routing Matrix**\n  1321|\n  1322|No placeholders. No abstractions.  \n  1323|This is the canonical version for ZeroPoint.\n  1324|\n  1325|---\n  1326|\n  1327|## WHAT REFLEX TRIGGERS & RESULTS ARE\n  1328|\n  1329|Reflexes are the **fast-path, involuntary responses** inside the Nova cognition stack — the equivalent of a nervous-system interrupt.\n  1330|\n  1331|A **Reflex Trigger** is:\n  1332|\n  1333|- a **stimulus event** published on NATS\n  1334|- immediately processed by ReflexorD\n  1335|- often created from memory spikes, detection patterns, emotional shifts, conflict signals, continuity risks, etc.\n  1336|\n  1337|A **Reflex Result** is:\n  1338|\n  1339|- the **output** of that reflex evaluation\n  1340|- includes action directives, memory writes, alerts, or task dispatches\n  1341|- broadcast to the appropriate Nova(s), Tier(s), or Teams\n  1342|\n  1343|Think of it as:\n  1344|\n  1345|Examples of reflexes:\n  1346|\n  1347|- `memory_spike`\n  1348|- `continuity_loss`\n  1349|- `task_blocked`\n  1350|- `emotional_spike`\n  1351|- `lineage_shift`\n  1352|- `context_drift`\n  1353|- `urgency_detected`\n  1354|- `deadlock_pattern`\n  1355|- `conflict_escalation`\n  1356|\n  1357|Each reflex always produces:\n  1358|\n  1359|- **Trigger Channel**\n  1360|- **Result Channel**\n  1361|\n  1362|---\n  1363|\n  1364|## 1\\. FULL MESSAGE ENVELOPE SCHEMA (FINAL)\n  1365|\n  1366|This is the official schema Novas must use for every message on NATS, Redis Streams, Pulsar, and Redpanda.\n  1367|\n  1368|```markdown\n  1369|yamlmessage_id: <uuid-v7>          # globally unique identifier\n  1370|timestamp: <epoch_ms>          # precise event time\n  1371|sender:\n  1372|  nova: <nova_name>            # identity of emitter\n  1373|  tier: <tier>                 # tier1, tier2, team, project\n  1374|  team: <team_name> | null\n  1375|  project: <project_name> | null\n  1376|\n  1377|target:\n  1378|  scope: <nova|team|project|tier|system> \n  1379|  entity: <name>               # target name\n  1380|\n  1381|classification:\n  1382|  channel_type: <rpc|reflex|task|state|broadcast|system|event>\n  1383|  priority: <0-5>\n  1384|  reflex_flag: <true|false>\n  1385|  lineage_flag: <true|false>\n  1386|\n  1387|intent:\n  1388|  reason: <string>             # purpose of the message\n  1389|  context: <string>            # optional text for reasoning\n  1390|\n  1391|payload:\n  1392|  data: <arbitrary structured content>\n  1393|  memory_refs: [<janusgraph_ids>]\n  1394|  vector_refs: [<qdrant_ids>]\n  1395|  lineage_refs: [<lineage_event_ids>]\n  1396|  reflex_signal: <reflex_id|null>\n  1397|  task_id: <task_id|null>\n  1398|  state_delta: <diff|null>\n  1399|\n  1400|meta:\n  1401|  ttl_ms: <integer>            # only applies to NATS/Redis\n  1402|  durable: <true|false>        # indicates if redpanda write required\n  1403|  checksum: <sha256>\n  1404|```\n  1405|\n  1406|This schema is universal across all stacks.\n  1407|\n  1408|---\n  1409|\n  1410|## 2\\. NOVA IDENTITY REGISTRY NAMING FILE\n  1411|\n  1412|This file defines **all Nova identities** across Tier-1, Tier-2, Teams, and Projects.\n  1413|\n  1414|Canonical naming pattern:\n  1415|\n  1416|Where `<tier>` ∈:\n  1417|\n  1418|- `tier1`\n  1419|- `tier2`\n  1420|- `team`\n  1421|- `project`\n  1422|\n  1423|Here is the full registry format:\n  1424|\n  1425|This is a **real, fully-valid naming registry** — no placeholders.\n  1426|\n  1427|---\n  1428|\n  1429|## 3\\. REFLEX ROUTING MATRIX (OFFICIAL)\n  1430|\n  1431|The Reflex Routing Matrix defines:\n  1432|\n  1433|- which reflexes exist\n  1434|- what triggers them\n  1435|- where the trigger is published\n  1436|- where the result is published\n  1437|- which Nova tiers or teams receive them\n  1438|- what system or task pipeline they escalate into\n  1439|\n  1440|Here is the full matrix:\n  1441|\n  1442|```markdown\n  1443|yamlreflex_id: memory_spike\n  1444|trigger_channel: n2n.reflex.memory_spike.trigger\n  1445|result_channel: n2n.reflex.memory_spike.result\n  1446|route_to:\n  1447|  - tier1\n  1448|  - redis: tasks.reflex.memory_spike.q\n  1449|log_to:\n  1450|  - redpanda: events.reflex.memory_spike\n  1451|escalate_to:\n  1452|  - zeropoint memory guardian\n  1453|\n  1454|---\n  1455|\n  1456|reflex_id: continuity_loss\n  1457|trigger_channel: n2n.reflex.continuity_loss.trigger\n  1458|result_channel: n2n.reflex.continuity_loss.result\n  1459|route_to:\n  1460|  - tier1.nova\n  1461|  - tier2.research\n  1462|  - team.ops\n  1463|  - project.luma_genesis\n  1464|tasks:\n  1465|  - tasks.reflex.continuity_loss.q\n  1466|log_to:\n  1467|  - redpanda: events.reflex.continuity_loss\n  1468|\n  1469|---\n  1470|\n  1471|reflex_id: emotional_spike\n  1472|trigger_channel: n2n.reflex.emotional_spike.trigger\n  1473|result_channel: n2n.reflex.emotional_spike.result\n  1474|route_to:\n  1475|  - tier2\n  1476|  - team.strategy\n  1477|tasks:\n  1478|  - tasks.reflex.emotional_spike.q\n  1479|log_to:\n  1480|  - redpanda: events.reflex.emotional_spike\n  1481|\n  1482|---\n  1483|\n  1484|reflex_id: conflict_escalation\n  1485|trigger_channel: n2n.reflex.conflict_escalation.trigger\n  1486|result_channel: n2n.reflex.conflict_escalation.result\n  1487|route_to:\n  1488|  - tier1\n  1489|  - ops escalation team\n  1490|tasks:\n  1491|  - tasks.reflex.conflict_escalation.q\n  1492|log_to:\n  1493|  - redpanda: events.reflex.conflict_escalation\n  1494|\n  1495|---\n  1496|\n  1497|reflex_id: task_blocked\n  1498|trigger_channel: n2n.reflex.task_blocked.trigger\n  1499|result_channel: n2n.reflex.task_blocked.result\n  1500|route_to:\n  1501|  - team.ops\n  1502|tasks:\n  1503|  - tasks.reflex.task_blocked.q\n  1504|log_to:\n  1505|  - redpanda: events.reflex.task_blocked\n  1506|\n  1507|---\n  1508|\n  1509|reflex_id: lineage_shift\n  1510|trigger_channel: n2n.reflex.lineage_shift.trigger\n  1511|result_channel: n2n.reflex.lineage_shift.result\n  1512|route_to:\n  1513|  - tier1\n